From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:28:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: add the MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4) panel record

Add the J604 internal panel to the firmware 26.6.2 board records.

The J604 runs the same DCP firmware image as the J713 (UUID
81BAF476-679D-3CC0-8C6A-E6B6FA659D5E), so its swap, completion and
open ABI is the J713's. Its own values:
- panel 3024x1964, with the preferred IOMFB timing element of the
  J604 under macOS (ID 2, 120 Hz, not virtual, no VRR):
  horizontal 3024/3104, front porch 8, sync 32, back porch 40,
  PreciseSyncRate 16986999; vertical 1964/2160, 102, 8, 86,
  PreciseSyncRate 7864351; the same single 8-bit color mode as the
  J713. That is an 804560 kHz pixel clock;
- 74 notch rows: m1n1 gives the notchless console 3024x1890;
- boot stride 12096, four bytes per pixel of the 3024-pixel console;
- 600 nits maximum, the user-accessible-max-nits of the J604 Apple
  device tree backlight (the J713 record keeps 500), and 140 nits for
  the first present, below the 300 nits thermal-mitigation cap.

Under macOS the J604 lists five more (ProMotion) timing elements next to
the preferred one. The backend accepts exactly one element, so if
firmware 26.6.2 lists them too the backend refuses the J604 session
rather than guessing a mode.

The record is only reached on a J604 whose loader hands the DCP over
and whose device tree enables it, which none does yet.

[dylan: the stride, the 140 nits level and the single timing element
 are not yet observed on a J604 running firmware 26.6.2]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
[dylan: tier c carries aurora a150a02ca3, whose swap_intent offset is part
 of the firmware 26.6.2 swap ABI like the other swap_* fields; the record
 takes the J713 value 0x17c on the same firmware-UUID basis, since without
 it the idle-cache registration would write its intent at offset 0.]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/Kconfig    | 11 ++++++-----
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/Kconfig b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/Kconfig
index 85eb4b496d..b27894fc72 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/Kconfig
@@ -42,16 +42,17 @@ config DRM_APPLE_DCP_T6030_AUDIO
 	  parser code exactly as before.
 
 config DRM_APPLE_DCP_T8132
-	bool "MacBook Air M4 (J713) internal panel"
+	bool "T8132 MacBook internal panel (J713, J604)"
 	depends on DRM_APPLE
 	depends on APPLE_DART=y && APPLE_DART_J713_DCP
 	depends on APPLE_PMP=y || APPLE_PMP=DRM_APPLE
 	select APERTURE_HELPERS
 	help
-	  Lets the common Apple display driver adopt the J713 (T8132)
-	  internal display coprocessor and its display subsystem. The
-	  inherited firmware session uses the IOMFB 26.6 interface, while
-	  planes, CRTCs, connectors and DMA GEM use the common DRM driver.
+	  Lets the common Apple display driver adopt the internal display
+	  coprocessor and display subsystem of the MacBook Air (13-inch, M4,
+	  J713) or MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4, J604). The inherited firmware
+	  session uses the IOMFB 26.6 interface, while planes, CRTCs,
+	  connectors and DMA GEM use the common DRM driver.
 
 	  The boot loader must publish the qualified firmware reservations
 	  and inherited display DART mappings. The retained session cannot
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 6fec59f6ca..53ea80e029 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -69,6 +69,33 @@ static const struct dcp_m4_profile dcp_m4_profiles[] = {
 			{ 1664, 1749, 33, 8, 44, 3932166, 1, 0 },
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		/*
+		 * MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4). Same DCP firmware image as the
+		 * J713, so the swap and callback ABI is that of the J713.
+		 * Panel and timing: the macOS IOMFB preferred element (ID 2,
+		 * 120 Hz); notch: m1n1's notchless console (1964 - 1890);
+		 * 600 nits: user-accessible-max-nits of the Apple device tree.
+		 * The 140 nits first-present level is a starting point below
+		 * the 300 nits thermal cap, not a measured default.
+		 */
+		.name = "J604",
+		.machine = "apple,j604",
+		.firmware_uuid = "81BAF476-679D-3CC0-8C6A-E6B6FA659D5E",
+		.panel_width = 3024, .panel_height = 1964, .notch_height = 74,
+		.boot_stride = 12096,
+		.swap_size = 0x1bd8, .swap_surface = 0x588, .swap_dva = 0xe38,
+		.swap_nullable = 0x1bcb, .swap_tail = 0x1bd6, .swap_nits = 0x35e,
+		.swap_intent = 0x17c,
+		.disabled_color = 0xff000000,
+		.done_method = 590, .done_size = 0x730, .open_method = 457,
+		.brightness_max = 600, .brightness_default = 140,
+		.width_mm = 0, .height_mm = 0,
+		.timing = {
+			{ 3024, 3104, 8, 32, 40, 16986999, 1, 0 },
+			{ 1964, 2160, 102, 8, 86, 7864351, 1, 0 },
+		},
+	},
 };
 
 const struct dcp_m4_profile *dcp_m4_pf __read_mostly = &dcp_m4_profiles[0];
